### Feature request

Is it possible to add 1 more field in the Op struct, to give clients more alternatives? For updates, `prevKv` can use much time, and possibly clients do not use it.

```
// Op represents an Operation that kv can execute.
type Op struct {
.....
	// for watch, put, delete
	prevKV bool
.....
}
```

```
type Op struct {
.....
	// for put
	prevKVforUpdate bool

// for delete
	prevKVforDelete bool
......
}
```

### Cause for this request

This applies to native etcd and to changed versions of etcd. When the K8s apiserver must get `PrevKv`, etcd must do a Range operation for each event. For native etcd, the Range operation operates on the local boltdb. Each Range operation is complete in less than 1s, approximately some ms. But all the Range operations together can use more than 1s.

The apiserver uses the code in etcd3/watcher.go to get all the objects of one type (for example Pod, Node or ConfigMap). This code does not use `oldObj`. Thus, for this code, you can remove the etcd operation that gets `PrevKv`.

